# `engines` in package.json is advisory by default: npm prints a warning and
# installs anyway. That is not enough here. `node:sqlite` is the entire
# persistence layer, it is still flagged experimental, and its API has moved
# across Node 22, 23 and 24 — so a mismatched runtime does not fail loudly, it
# produces a database call that behaves one way locally and another way on the
# droplet. The suite goes green on a major production has never run.
#
# This makes the range in `package.json` (`>=22.23.2 <23`) binding: npm refuses
# to install rather than warn. The same version is in `.nvmrc` and in
# `.github/workflows/verify.yml`, and all three move together.
#
# If an install fails here, that is this file working. Install the pinned
# version — `nvm install` in the repo root reads `.nvmrc`, as do `fnm` and
# `asdf` — rather than removing the flag.
#
# See docs/setup.md, "The Node version, and the divergence to fix".
engine-strict=true
